    {
      "input": "Thanks *he said to them, after which he decides to give them back the boots*\nYou'll need them more than me",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Nicco spoke to empty air, gesturing vaguely toward where he thought someone stood. In Heartstone Square, a few passers-by glanced his way at the words—*Thanks* and *You'll need them more than me*—but found only a heavyset stranger with thinning hair and premature white strands, apparently addressing nothing. No boots left his hands. None were offered.\n\nLivia Marr, small and narrow-framed with casually pinned dark-blond hair, had stopped a few paces away to adjust a strap on her shoulder. She heard him speak, measured the scene in a glance—his empty hands, the absence of any recipient—and let out a single amused breath through her nose. She pulled a pin from between her lips, recaptured it with three others, and held her position at the edge of the square's moderate foot traffic, watching with quick, perceptive eyes but making no approach.\n\nThe leather boots she had carried remained at her side, unseen by him, unmentioned by her.",
